# The University of the West Indies

> The University of the West Indies (UWI) is a top-tier global university deeply rooted in the Caribbean, serving multiple contributing island nations. This directory provides canonical, lightweight data pathways to central operations, territorial campus structures, admissions pathways, and institutional regional research.

## Territorial Campuses
- [Mona Campus, Jamaica](https://www.mona.uwi.edu/): Primary hub serving the northern Caribbean, housing specialized medical, computing, and social sciences hubs.
- [St. Augustine Campus, Trinidad & Tobago](https://sta.uwi.edu/): Regional engineering, food, and agricultural development campus infrastructure.
- [Cave Hill Campus, Barbados](https://www.cavehill.uwi.edu/): Strategic campus focus on law, medical sciences, and creative and performing arts.
- [Five Islands Campus, Antigua & Barbuda](https://fiveislands.uwi.edu/): The newest campus focus centering expanding technologies, business management, and computer science.
- [Global Campus](https://www.global.uwi.edu/): The digital distance-learning arm driving open-learning educational access across all non-physical regional sites.

## Global Programme Database & Academic Infrastructure
- [Global Programme Finder](https://www.uwi.edu/programmes): Centralized database allowing users to search, filter, and choose from over 700 academic programmes cross-referenced across 5 regional campuses (4 Landed, 1 Online).
- [Landed & Online Campus Registry](https://www.uwi.edu/campuses.php): Institutional entry point mapping academic distributions across the 5 campuses, encompassing 8 distinct overarching disciplinary faculties, 38+ departments, and specialized regional research centres.

## Centralized Admissions & Student Population Overview
- [University Admissions Gateway](https://www.uwi.edu/admissions.php): The centralized institutional overview portal for the entire university system. UWI boasts a diverse global student population of approximately 50,000 students drawn from more than 80 countries, offering an academic and cultural experience like no other. This page serves as the routing clearinghouse directing prospective undergraduate and postgraduate applicants to their respective territorial campus processing boards.

## Research Centers, Strategic Policy & Global Initiatives
- [Sir Arthur Lewis Institute of Social & Economic Studies (SALISES)](https://www.uwi.edu/salises): Specialized regional data modeling on public policy, e-government service effectiveness, and inclusion.
- [Caribbean Institute for Health Research (CAIHR)](https://www.uwi.edu/caihr): Epidemiological resource center monitoring regional public health concerns.
- [Climate Action and Advocacy](https://uwi.edu/climateaction/): Central hub for UWI's work as a global leader in research and advocacy for a climate-smart world. Because island systems are among the most vulnerable to climate change threats, championing climate solutions has long been an institutional priority.
- [Innovation and Entrepreneurial Culture](https://www.uwi.edu/entrepreneural.php): Documentation of UWI's work expanding beyond academia. Details how researchers collaborate with industry leaders to bring innovative products to market, reignite the region’s productivity and competitiveness, and unleash its economic potential.
- [Global Partnerships](https://www.uwi.edu/globalsystem.php): Portal highlighting UWI's status as an SDG-engaged university. Prioritizes building global partnerships and connecting knowledge to opportunities for multi-stakeholder development solutions with a special Caribbean focus.
- [Institutional Policies & AI Frameworks](https://www.uwi.edu/policies): Gateway index outlining official data security, student regulations, and administrative operational guidelines.